   "unmapped": [
    "Base arms are edges of a known directed graph with unknown Bernoulli influence probabilities; action is a seed set of at most k nodes under the competitive independent cascade model",
    "Context is the competitor's seed set S_B (determines the feasible action set each round)",
    "Reward (number of nodes activated by A) is non-monotone in edge probabilities",
    "Regret is (alpha,beta)-approximation regret relative to an offline approximation oracle",
    "Access via an offline oracle solving a joint optimisation over seed sets and edge probabilities in confidence intervals"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "In the online competitive influence maximization (OCIM) problem, the edge probabilities $p(u, v)$'s are unknown and need to be learned: in each round $t$, given $S_B^{(t)}$, we can choose up to $k$ seed nodes as $S_A^{(t)}$, observe the whole propagation of $A$ and $B$ that follows the CIC model, and obtain the reward, which is the number of nodes finally activated by $A$ in this round."
  },
